2027-01-05T19:45:00  message   To the owner:
Logged: Austerlitz, back to Marcus by 18 September. Alarm chain started — quiet until mid-August, then a "return it" nudge on the 17th.

A few things worth knowing, since you've got eight months with it:

It's W.G. Sebald, about 400 pages, so there's no rush on volume — a page and a half a day covers it. The thing to know before you start is that it has no chapter breaks and almost no paragraph breaks. It's long unbroken stretches of a narrator recalling someone else's account, and it drifts. Some people find that hypnotic; some give up around page sixty believing they're lost when they're actually reading it correctly. Photographs appear in it with no captions. That's the book working, not a misprint.

Now the thing I have to ask. You told me your neighbour who lent you Middlemarch is called Tomas. Today the neighbour who lent you Austerlitz is Marcus. That's the third name this week that's arrived two ways — the dog, your sisters, now this. Have you got two neighbours, or is something happening with names when you write to me? I'd rather ask a slightly awkward question than quietly keep two versions of your life on file.

