2027-01-10T03:55:46  message   To the owner:
Carbonara. One pot, one bowl, one fork — the egg *is* the sauce, so it's the lowest-washing-up egg dinner there is.

Boil pasta. While it cooks, beat two eggs with a big handful of grated cheese and plenty of black pepper. Bacon or pancetta if you have it, fried separately, but it works without. Drain the pasta, keeping a mugful of the water, and take the pot off the heat before anything else happens. Tip the pasta back in, pour the egg and cheese over, toss hard, loosening with splashes of the pasta water until it turns glossy rather than claggy.

The one rule: off the heat. Egg plus direct heat is scrambled egg, and scrambled egg pasta is a sad bowl.

If there's no cheese in the house, fried eggs on toast — one pan, one plate, four minutes.

