2027-01-10T04:09:33  message   To the owner:
Short version, since you got the long one on Tuesday: it's leftover kitten behaviour.

Kneading is what a kitten does on its mother to get milk flowing, and the motion stays wired in for life. Cats do it on soft things when they're relaxed and content — it's a comfort habit, the cat equivalent of fidgeting with something familiar.

Two extras: they have scent glands between the pads, so kneading also marks the blanket as theirs. And it's usually paired with purring, which is why it looks so pleased with itself.

