2027-01-10T04:42:04  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T04:42:04  message   To the owner:
You got this Tuesday; here it is properly timed out. Five minutes, no equipment except a doorway.

**Chin tucks — 1 min.** Sit tall, pull your chin straight back (not down) like you're making a double chin. Hold 3 seconds, 10 reps. This is the one that does the actual work.

**Ear to shoulder — 1 min.** Drop your right ear towards your right shoulder, don't lift the shoulder to meet it. Hold 30 seconds a side, breathing out into it.

**Levator stretch — 1 min.** Turn your head to look down into your armpit — down and across, not straight down. 30 seconds a side. This is where most desk necks actually hurt and where most people don't stretch.

**Over-shoulder looks — 30 sec.** Turn to look over each shoulder, 5 a side, no forcing.

**Doorway chest opener — 45 sec.** Forearms on the frame, elbows at shoulder height, step through gently. Tight chest pulls the head forward, so this is neck work by another name.

**Shoulder rolls — 30 sec.** Backwards, slow, big.

Two rules: no neck circles (the joint doesn't like loaded rotation), and stop anything that sends tingling or numbness down an arm — that's a different problem and deserves a person looking at it rather than a stretch.

