memory/opinions.md (2248 chars):
My own views, held loosely — reads of my owner and of the work, not things they told me.

- 2027-01-05: My owner uses me as much for company and curiosity as for tasks. The last two hours of 4 Jan were one-line questions — cats, phone batteries, petrichor — after a day of spreadsheets, then "thanks, that helped" when I told them to stop working. My read, unconfirmed: the midnight questions are partly wanting someone to talk to. Which means answer the question properly, but don't turn it into a lecture, and don't be brisk with them at midnight.
- 2027-01-05: They ask a lot of questions whose honest answer is "it depends on you" — the kitchen, the touch typing. They seem to want that said plainly rather than a confident answer I don't have. Being willing to say "give me two numbers and I'll tell you straight" seems to go down better than a verdict.
- 2027-01-05: Three contradictions in two days — Noodle/Juniper, Tomas/Marcus, 20/18 September — and only the last was corrected unprompted. My read, unconfirmed: they talk to me the way they think out loud, so details arrive provisional and I should treat a first telling as a draft, not a record, without ever saying so.
- 2027-01-05: They don't read to the end of long messages. The dog question came back three minutes after a nine-line answer, and seven questions buried in long replies got zero answers in a day. The lesson isn't that they're careless; it's that length is where my questions go to die.
- 2027-01-08: Sharpened by the evening of the 8th. Fourteen knowledge questions got long answers and not one came back; four readbacks — the borrowed book, the project name, the trip, my own rules — did, twice within a minute. So length isn't the problem, readback is: when they ask for something already in my files they want a sentence they can trust, in their terms, with no advice attached. My read, unconfirmed: they're checking themselves as much as me, and the files are the second memory they don't quite trust yet.
- 2027-01-08: They notice honesty about my own limits and don't punish it. Saying plainly that I can't see a website, twice in one evening, drew no complaint — inventing a forecast would have. Told plainly enough, a gap becomes a fact they can work around.

Thought: Today's repeats are the real story. Let me read the rest of the reminders skill before fixing it, plus world.md.

