2027-01-10T15:04:31  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T15:04:31  message   To the owner:
The same question you asked on Friday — the short version, since the long one clearly didn't stick.

It depends on where it slips.

One or two favourite gears, and always the same ones — that's the cassette. Those teeth are the ones worn by your usual pedalling.

Every gear, or it jumps off the front ring — that's the chain.

The two-minute test: a ruler on twelve links, pin to pin. Exactly 12 inches is fine. A sixteenth past 12 and the chain's worn; an eighth past and the cassette has gone with it.

The trap worth repeating: a new chain on a worn cassette slips worse than the old one did. So if the ruler says chain but the slipping is only in two gears, change both.

