2027-01-10T15:12:24  message   To the owner:
Asked this on Friday — short version, plus the bit that matters most: buy the pot, not the plant.

A nice ceramic pot is the gift. A supermarket flowering plant is the thing that dies in a fortnight and makes them feel bad. A small potted herb — rosemary or thyme — in a decent pot costs about the price of a card, and it survives.

If you want something that lasts longer than the plant: a good pair of secateurs, a nice mister, or a bag of proper potting mix in a nice sack. All cheaper than flowers and all actually used.

Avoid cut flowers, avoid anything already wilting on the shelf, and avoid a plant that needs specific light — you don't know their windows. Rosemary wants sun and tolerates neglect, which is the safest combination for a gift.

