2027-01-10T15:35:30  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T15:35:30  message   To the owner:
Asked this yesterday — 42%, give or take.

Exactly 91 in 216. The easy way to see it: the chance of *no* six on one die is 5/6, so on three it's 5/6 × 5/6 × 5/6 = 125/216, just under 58%. Everything else has at least one six, which leaves 91/216, a shade over 42%.

The intuition that trips people: it feels like it should be 50%, because three dice and a one-in-six chance. It isn't, and it doesn't get to even odds until you roll four (52%).

